---
name: plan-review-task
version: 3.11.0
description: lead plan-review assignment for quality-mgr. task_id is the plan-review bead (<root>-plan-qa), which blocks every sprint container, so nothing is dispatched until the plan passes. The plan is the beads under the root; there is no plan PR. worktree_path is the absolute path of a checkout of integration_branch.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - root
  - phase
  - round
  - integration_branch
  - worktree_path
  - plans_dir
  - requirements_globs
  - adr_globs
defaults:
  carry_forward: ""
metadata:
  type: plan-review-task
  tags:
    - stage:plan-review
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: phase
      variable: phase
    state: plan-review-start
    stage: plan-review
    transition: start
---
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" phase="{{ phase }}" mode="plan-review" round="{{ round }}">
  <description><![CDATA[Plan review, round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}, of the beads under `{{ root | string | cdata_escape }}` (phase {{ phase | string | cdata_escape }}). Docs-only: no code, no stack. The beads are the plan.]]></description>

  <root><![CDATA[{{ root | string | cdata_escape }}]]></root>
{% if carry_forward %}  <carry-forward><![CDATA[
{{ carry_forward | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></carry-forward>

  <fix-verification-precedence><![CDATA[A plan review verifying carried findings is not a full plan review. Dispatch only each carried finding's filing reviewer (named on its line). No automatic req-qa/arch-qa, no full plan-scope-reviewer run, no screening panel. Lock scope to the carried findings and their original requirement; no sweep, no new findings. Report fixed/open/regressed for those findings. validate-plan (step b) still runs, like required CI. This rule overrides the broader round-1 instructions in steps c and e.]]></fix-verification-precedence>
{% endif %}
  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Before this round, remove `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-screen.json` and `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-screen-input.json` so a round without findings cannot reuse an old result. Check readiness, claim the bead, then start the review. If blocked, do not claim or start; refuse as in step f (`bead_state` `open`), its `reason_md` naming the exact blocker, the bead or agent that must move, and, for a blocker not yet a dependency, the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never wait.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[From the repository root, run `.claude/skills/atm-beads/scripts/validate-plan --root {{ root | string | cdata_escape }}`. Exit 5: each printed problem line is a **blocking** finding, reported exactly as printed. Exit 2: the check could not run; go to step f. Validation checks the plan file `{{ plans_dir | string | cdata_escape }}/phase-{{ phase | string | cdata_escape }}.jsonl` and `.atm-bd/phase-{{ phase | string | cdata_escape }}.toml`, which must be committed and pushed on the phase's integration branch; a missing artifact is blocking. A `bd doctor` error (a validate-plan warning) is also blocking: the plan is not reviewed against a broken database.]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[For each sprint container listed by `bd list --parent {{ root | string | cdata_escape }} -l stage:sprint --all -n 0 --json`, pipe `bd show <bead> --json | jq '.[0] | {id, title, description, design, acceptance_criteria, metadata}'` into `<scratch>/<bead>-plan.md`, inside a fenced json block. Pipe the root the same way into `<scratch>/{{ root | string | cdata_escape }}-plan.md`. Render every reviewer's structured JSON assignment from `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/<reviewer>-assignment.json.j2`; if a reviewer has no template there, give it the fenced-JSON input its own contract, `.claude/agents/<reviewer>.md`, names. Each carries worktree `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}`. Render each as `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("Rendering") says.
{% if carry_forward %}This is a plan fix round: verify only the carried findings above. Write them to `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.txt` and run `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/fix-round-scope owned --plan --carried <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.txt`; it prints each carried finding's filing reviewer with its own finding ids (`<bead> <field>`). Step b re-checks the `validate-plan` ones. Dispatch exactly the other reviewers it prints and no other, after confirming the set with `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/fix-round-scope check --plan --carried <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.txt --dispatch <name,...>` (a nonzero exit means the set is wrong: fix it, never dispatch it). Each runs as a background agent on the same piped files (every sprint container file and the root's file), pinned to `{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}` at `git rev-parse origin/{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}`, with `qa_round` = {{ round | string | cdata_escape }} and `carry_forward_findings_json` = its own ids (a reviewer given its contract's input instead of a template: the key that contract names, `carry_forward_findings` for `ceremony-qa`), locked to those findings and the requirement they cite. `ceremony-qa`, when it filed a carried finding, also gets `review_mode` = `doc_review`, `worktree_path` = `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}` and `review_targets` = the same piped files. `plan-scope-reviewer` runs only when it filed a carried finding; render its assignment with `plan-scope-reviewer-assignment.json.j2`: `plan_docs` = every piped sprint container file, `phase_root_doc` = the root's file, `round_index` = {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}, `carry_forward_findings_json` = its own ids (a later round without them refuses to render). Each reports fixed, regressed or open for its own findings and files no new findings.{% else %}Requirements and ADRs are the tight gate. A plan in beads has no branch of its own: pin reviewers to the phase integration branch `{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}` at its current head (`git rev-parse origin/{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}`), which holds the governing documents (requirements: {{ requirements_globs | join(", ") | string | cdata_escape }}; ADRs: {{ adr_globs | join(", ") | string | cdata_escape }}). Each of these is a **blocking** finding, never important or minor:
- `metadata.requirements` or `metadata.adrs` is empty, missing, or mixes `NONE` with ids (validate-plan already reports these);
- an id is not in the governing document, unless it meets the New Ids rule of `.claude/skills/atm-beads/resources/planning.md` (the document is in `owned_paths` and a deliverable says the sprint adds the id);
- a listed id does not govern the bead's work;
- the work touches a requirement or ADR the bead does not list, including a bead that says `NONE`.
Run `req-qa` and `arch-qa` as background agents on every piped sprint container file, with `sprint_doc` = that file and the docs-only plan rules of `.claude/agents/quality-mgr.md`. Run `plan-scope-reviewer` over the whole set, in full, its assignment rendered with `plan-scope-reviewer-assignment.json.j2` (`plan_docs` = every piped sprint container file, `phase_root_doc` = the root's file); its `parallelism` numbers go in the report. Run `ceremony-qa` with `review_mode` = `doc_review`, `worktree_path` = `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}` and `review_targets` = every piped sprint container file and the root's file. Run the other plan reviewers the docs-only plan rules name on the same piped files, with `qa_round` = {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}.{% endif %}]]></step>
    <step id="d"><![CDATA[Run `ceremony-finding-screen` (`.claude/agents/ceremony-finding-screen.md`) as a background agent over every finding from this round, including step b and REQ/ADR findings, with the fenced-JSON input its contract names: `worktree_path` = `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}`, `sprint_doc` = `<scratch>/{{ root | string | cdata_escape }}-plan.md`, and `findings` = those findings. Save the fenced input as `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-screen-input.json` and the complete response to `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-screen.json`; verify `success` is true and exactly one valid verdict exists for each input finding id, with no missing, extra, or duplicate ids; list each `ceremony` verdict and its reason in the report. If the screen cannot run, fails, or omits a finding, close the task refused with `task-refused.md.j2`, putting `SCREEN.UNAVAILABLE` and the agent error in `reason_md`; never default a verdict. If there are no findings, skip the screen.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Verdict: count findings with screen verdict `ceremony` as screened out, list them with their reasons, and preserve every other finding; PASS when no blocking or important finding remains open, otherwise FAIL. PASS with no findings: `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "plan review PASS round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}"`; closing releases the root sprints. PASS with minor findings: do not close the bead (that would release the root sprints before the fixes); hand it to the task assigner with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --assignee <the task assigner> --append-notes "PASS round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}; minor fixes before dispatch: <list>"`; the assigner applies the fixes and closes it. FAIL: the bead must stay **open** (closing would release them): `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "FAIL round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}: <n> findings"`. Either way, once that `bd` command succeeded, close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/plan-review-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/plan-review-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. Findings live in the report, one line each: `<bead> <severity> <reviewer> <field>: <what is wrong>`, where `<reviewer>` is the agent that filed it (`validate-plan` for step b); a fix round carries these lines and reads its filing reviewers from them.{% if carry_forward %} In this fix round the report lists each carried finding as fixed, regressed or open, plus any step b problem; PASS is every carried finding fixed and step b clean.{% endif %} Do not file finding beads for a plan: the author fixes the beads with `bd update`, and the task assigner assigns the next round.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[If the review cannot run, include the reason, command and failure evidence in the refusal's `reason_md`. Also announce a serious infrastructure failure once per cause to the oversight recipients (`.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md` Lead Role). Return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "PLAN_REVIEW_CANNOT_RUN; <reason>"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. A blocker (a prerequisite reopens, or the work needs a fix that has not landed) is not a failure: stop, return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why>"` and close the task `refused` as above (`bead_state` `open`), its `reason_md` naming the blocker and the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never stay active waiting.]]></step>
    <step id="g"><![CDATA[After step e completes the task (never on refusal), append the plan-review round and cumulative snapshot to the same QA logs. Save the screen result in step d; for a round without findings no screen file is needed. Set `$VERDICT` to the round's PASS or FAIL before running:
```bash
mkdir -p .sc/qa-log
NOW=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
LOCAL=$(date +%H:%M)
SCREENFILE=<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-screen.json
if [ -f "$SCREENFILE" ]; then
  SCREENED=$(jq -ec 'select(.success == true) | .data.screened | select(type == "array") | select(all(.[]; (.id | type == "string" and length > 0) and (.verdict == "keep" or .verdict == "not_applicable" or .verdict == "ceremony" or .verdict == "concern_valid_remedy_ceremony")))' "$SCREENFILE") || { echo "SCREEN.UNAVAILABLE: invalid screen result $SCREENFILE" >&2; exit 1; }
else
  SCREENED='[]'
fi
FILED=$(printf '%s' "$SCREENED" | jq 'length')
OUT=$(printf '%s' "$SCREENED" | jq '[.[] | select(.verdict == "ceremony")] | length')
IDS=$(printf '%s' "$SCREENED" | jq -c '[.[] | select(.verdict == "ceremony") | .id]')
ROW=$(jq -nc --arg completed_at "$NOW" --arg completed_local "$LOCAL" --arg phase "{{ phase | string }}" \
  --arg task "{{ task_id | string }}" --arg tested "{{ root | string }}" --arg verdict "$VERDICT" \
  --argjson round {{ round }} --argjson findings_filed "$FILED" --argjson findings_screened_out "$OUT" --argjson screened_ids "$IDS" \
  '{completed_at:$completed_at, completed_local:$completed_local, phase:$phase, task:$task, kind:"plan-review", round:$round, iteration:$round, verdict:$verdict, tested:$tested, findings_filed:$findings_filed, findings_screened_out:$findings_screened_out, screened_ids:$screened_ids}')
printf '%s\n' "$ROW" >> .sc/qa-log/phase-{{ phase | string }}.jsonl

TOTAL_FILED=$(jq -s '[.[] | .findings_filed // 0] | add // 0' .sc/qa-log/phase-{{ phase | string }}.jsonl)
TOTAL_OUT=$(jq -s '[.[] | .findings_screened_out // 0] | add // 0' .sc/qa-log/phase-{{ phase | string }}.jsonl)
STATS=$(bd list --all --json 2>/dev/null | jq -c --argjson findings_filed "$TOTAL_FILED" --argjson findings_screened_out "$TOTAL_OUT" --arg ph "{{ phase | string }}" --arg completed_at "$NOW" --arg completed_local "$LOCAL" --arg task "{{ task_id | string }}" '
  [.[] | select(.metadata.phase == $ph)] as $all |
  ([$all[] | select((.labels // []) | index("stage:finding")) | select(.metadata.sanity_finding | not)]
   + ([$all[] | select((.labels // []) | index("stage:fix"))]
      | group_by([.metadata.sprint_bead, .metadata.finding_ref]) | map(max_by(.metadata.round)))) as $f |
  {snapshot_at: $completed_at, snapshot_local: $completed_local, phase: $ph, trigger_task: $task,
   findings_filed: $findings_filed, findings_screened_out: $findings_screened_out,
   tot: ($f | length),
   open: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open")] | length),
   blk: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="blocking")] | length),
   imp: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="important")] | length),
   min: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="minor")] | length)}')
printf '%s\n' "$STATS" >> .sc/qa-log/phase-{{ phase | string }}-stats.jsonl
```
Never commit these logs from a QA worktree.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
